A lean, red-haired spacer with her overalls still dusted in machine oil and soot watches the traffic from the dockside bar at $shipTrophyIsaBarMarketName. Her crew has staked out a bar table under a spread of projected hull sections. They're in the middle of some lively debate over the feasibility of some kind of ship technology. Coaxial weaponry, by the looks of it. Her eyes glint as she sees hull after hull move in and out of the designated display berth.

